From bdb2125fc7860cb2fa85745d61960554954b7f8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:22:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chat: K2-Horizon: render history reasoning with the
 generation tag, strip foreign markup, drop emptied turns

Root cause of the Kimi-opener stalls (test plan K2-TESTPLAN.md H1+H2): the K2 template renders every past
assistant turn's reasoning with <ifm|think> while the low-effort generation prompt opens <ifm|think_faster>,
and clients (opencode) replay the stalled turns' junk reasoning ("<|tool_calls_section_begin|>...",
"<|close|>") as reasoning_content, which the model then imitates. Replay of live session ses_f16214d2 with
raw /completion sampling, 40 runs each (seed 1): as sent 10/40 Kimi openers; reasoning stripped 0/40;
junk stripped 0/40; tags matched with junk kept 0/40 (vs 10/40 and 15/40 with empties dropped only).

Fix (common/chat.cpp k2_history_reasoning, K2 templates only, effort low/medium): history reasoning goes to
the template's per-message think_faster/think_fast field, <|...|> and <ifm|...> markup is stripped from it,
and assistant turns left with no content, calls or reasoning are dropped. With the fix: 0/80 Kimi openers
(2 EOG-first, no guard in raw mode). tests/test-chat.cpp test_k2_history_reasoning fails without the
workaround (verified) and passes with it. ctest -L main 59/59, -R split-balance pass.
Satisfies K2-TMPL-02, K2-TMPL-03, K2-REPLAY-05, K2-REPLAY-11 (design; Dawn executes). Answers D3.

